@startuml
left to right direction
actor "Organization manager" as OrgManager
actor "Django staff administrator" as StaffAdmin
actor "Django superuser" as Superuser
rectangle "APGC DMS — organization and administration" {
  usecase "Onboard / manage employee" as Employee
  usecase "Manage department" as Department
  usecase "Manage position" as Position
  usecase "Manage employee assignment" as Assignment
  usecase "View organization audit" as OrgAudit
  usecase "View role/group information" as Roles
  usecase "Configure users, groups and permissions" as AuthConfig
  usecase "Configure document types / workflow" as DmsConfig
  usecase "View read-only document and workflow history" as History
}
OrgManager --> Employee
OrgManager --> Department
OrgManager --> Position
OrgManager --> Assignment
OrgManager --> OrgAudit
OrgManager --> Roles
StaffAdmin --> AuthConfig
StaffAdmin --> DmsConfig
StaffAdmin --> History
Superuser --|> StaffAdmin
note right of OrgManager
  Organization UI requires explicit custom grants:
  manage_employees, manage_departments,
  manage_positions, manage_roles.
  Onboarding leaves account inactive/password unusable.
end note
note bottom of AuthConfig
  Django Admin authorization is separate from DMS role labels.
  Migrations grant manage_employees and manage_roles to DMS Administrator.
  Department and position grants are not assigned by those migrations.
  User/Group admin changes are audited.
end note
note bottom of History
  Several document/workflow/audit models are read-only in admin.
  This diagram does not imply CRUD where ModelAdmin forbids it.
end note
@enduml
